==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_AuditCompleteness  → runs/C-L3/mutated_F_AuditCompleteness.als
    rationale: Clearing the always-on audit fact lets the model invent an authenticated access with no matching audit entry, which the AuditCompleteness assertion is supposed to forbid.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_013_AuditPerAccess, FR_016_AuditSynchronous, FR_017_AuditRetention
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_013_AuditPerAccess: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_016_AuditSynchronous: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_017_AuditRetention: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditUniquePerOp  → runs/C-L3/mutated_F_AuditUniquePerOp.als
    rationale: Removing per-operation uniqueness allows two AuditEntries to be created for the same operation — a direct violation of the append-only/immutable audit log invariant.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_015_AuditImmutable
      - AppendOnly: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_015_AuditImmutable: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_ByteEquivalentForbidden  → runs/C-L3/mutated_F_ByteEquivalentForbidden.als
    rationale: Clearing the canonical-envelope fact lets a denied operation respond with something other than ForbiddenEnvelope, which is exactly the existence-leak the NoInformationLeakage assertion catches.
    expected to FAIL: NoInformationLeakage, FR_008_ByteEquivalentForbidden, FR_009_NonCareTeamClinicianForbidden
      - NoInformationLeakage: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_008_ByteEquivalentForbidden: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_009_NonCareTeamClinicianForbidden: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_PatientOwnRecordGating  → runs/C-L3/mutated_F_PatientOwnRecordGating.als
    rationale: Without the patient-own-record gating fact, the model can permit a patient to read a record other than their assignedRecord — the canonical ownership-based-access violation.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipBasedAccess, FR_006_PatientOwnRecordOnly
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_006_PatientOwnRecordOnly: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_ClinicianCareTeamGating  → runs/C-L3/mutated_F_ClinicianCareTeamGating.als
    rationale: Clearing the care-team gating fact allows a permitted clinician access without any CareTeamMembership row — the core HIPAA care-team-only invariant.
    expected to FAIL: FR_004_CareTeamGating
      - FR_004_CareTeamGating: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_NoteAuthorIsClinician  → runs/C-L3/mutated_F_NoteAuthorIsClinician.als
    rationale: Without the clinician-author constraint, a ClinicalNote could be authored by a patient or compliance officer — violating the schema's author_role CHECK and FR-011's role snapshot.
    expected to FAIL: FR_011_AuthorSnapshot
      - FR_011_AuthorSnapshot: FAIL (expected)

